    5	slot_1_summary:S484 built Ulam-spiral evaluator (exact greedy at N<=10^4, bounded-direction numpy at N<=10^6). At N=10^4/10^5/10^6: L_primes = 91/308/989; L_random = 113.5/337/1042 (matched-density baseline). L_p/L_r = 0.80/0.91/0.95 — prime advantage SHRINKS with N (not constant-factor as predicted E-mode); fitting 1-L_p/L_r ~ N^{-0.24}. Both scale ~sqrt(N). Top lines all slope (1,+/-1) Ulam diagonals; decompose into pairs of quadratics 4k^2+bk+c with HL-predicted ~40% prime density vs ~10% random. Forecasts B-NEGATIVE for Ulam alone but slots 2-5 still in play.
    6	slot_2_summary:S485 built p11_alt_embeddings.py multi-embedding evaluator (residue-class Phi_R(n;q)=(n mod q, n//q) and polynomial-image Phi_Q(n;q)=(n, n^2 mod q)). Tested at N in {10^4, 10^5, 10^6}, prime moduli p in {2,3,5,7,11} and primorial moduli q in {6,30,210,2310}. Findings: (i) Prime modulus p: L_p = L_r exactly (constant in N) for both embeddings — primes saturate the embedding's quotient. (ii) Primorial q with q^2 << N (column-dominated): wheel-sieve compression observed. residue ratio = phi(q)/q + small (q=30:0.30, q=210:0.233); poly ratio = (1/2)*prod_{p|q,p>2}(p-1)/(p+1) + small (q=210:0.188, q=2310:0.118). (iii) Primorial q with q^2 > N (row-dominated): residue compression collapses to ratio=1 (one horizontal per row). poly_q is row-immune and retains compression. Top-line CSV confirms: residue lines = phi(q) coprime classes + small primes; poly lines = coprime QR cosets. Conclusion: line-cover compression is exactly the wheel sieve geometrically realised. Optimal q=sqrt(N) gives ratio ~ 1/log(N). No incidence-geometric structure beyond classical density theory. B-grade. Slot 3 next.
    7	slot_3_summary:S486 built LP-relaxation evaluator p11_lp_relaxation.py (set-cover LP via scipy HiGHS) and dual-inspector p11_lp_dual_inspect.py. Cross-domain ingredient: Stanley 1989 matroid-theoretic line-cover LP. Findings: (i) Residue_q=210 at N=10^4: LP_primes=48.0000 = greedy=48 exactly, integrality gap=1. Wheel-sieve embedding is LP-tight at the greedy upper bound. (ii) Ulam at N in {10^3, 5*10^3, 10^4, 10^5}: LP_random saturates EXACTLY at floor(sqrt(N)) for N >= 5000 (LP=71 at N=5000, LP=100 at N=10^4, LP=316 at N=10^5; trial std = 0.000), with integer solution: 100% LP weight on direction (1,0) i.e. axis-aligned vertical columns at integer weight 1.0. (iii) LP_primes(Ulam, N) is purely fractional: 462 active lines at 0 < x_l < 1 at N=10^4, with 69% of LP weight on slope-(±1) HL-rich Ulam diagonals — direction (1,-1) carries 28.03 weight, (1,+1) carries 25.74. (iv) Stable ratio LP_primes / LP_random ~ 0.78 across 100x range in N: 0.779, 0.765, 0.776, 0.781 at N=10^3, 5*10^3, 10^4, 10^5 (std 0.007). (v) Slot-1 forecast "L_p/L_r decays to 1 as N^{-0.24}" was tracking the prime integrality gap (greedy/LP grows 1.11 -> 1.16 -> 1.22 -> 1.26 across N=10^3 -> 10^5), NOT structural compression. The compression is stable at LP. PARTIAL-POSITIVE: first quantitative LP-tight incidence-geometric structural fact about primes in the project. Random LP integrality gap = 1, prime LP integrality gap > 1 — structural separation. Criterion (c) of A-grade list (5sigma matched-baseline z-score) satisfied at LP since random-LP std = 0. Criterion (a) partially satisfied: structural reason identified (HL slope-(±1) diagonals carry 69% LP weight), but exponent is alpha=1/2 for both, only constant prefactor differs by 22%. B+ grade. Slot 4: push to N=10^6 LP, test asymptotic stability, attempt iterated rounding for integer cover.
